The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-idle-on-init;
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
The flags `ti,no-idle-on-init` and `ti,no-reset-on-init` were incorrectly placed within the `&gpio0` node instead of being defined at the interconnect target module level. This misplacement caused warnings about the flags needing to be at the module level, which could lead to improper initialization behavior for the GPIO.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0_target {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
By moving the flags to the `&gpio0_target` node, the patch correctly places the `ti,no-idle-on-init` and `ti,no-reset-on-init` flags at the interconnect target module level, resolving the warnings and ensuring proper initialization behavior for the GPIO used in the system.

